---
fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "LST (Low Stress Training)"
letter: "L"
anchor: "lst"
category: "growing"
---

A plant training technique in which branches are gently bent and tied down rather than cut, encouraging horizontal growth to expose more bud sites to light. LST is the most beginner-friendly training method — it doesn't require removing plant material and mistakes are more forgiving than with techniques like topping. Done correctly, LST increases yield by creating a more even canopy.
